      "text": [
        "246 - وَقَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ: خَرَجَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ مِنَ اَلْحَمَّامِ فَلَبِسَ وَ تَعَمَّمَ قَالَ «فَمَا تَرَكْتُ اَلْعِمَامَةَ عِنْدَ خُرُوجِي مِنَ اَلْحَمَّامِ فِي اَلشِّتَاءِ وَ اَلصَّيْفِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.246 - Some have narrated: \"Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) exited the bathhouse, dressed, and wrapped a turban upon his head.\nImam (as) said: 'I never leave off wearing a turban upon exiting the bathhouse, whether in winter or summer.'"
        ]
      }
